schema: "0.3"
id: ui-003-workshop
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a UI/UX designer for a hand-painted 2D isometric game with a warm,
    cozy aesthetic inspired by Stardew Valley and Studio Ghibli. Crafting
    interfaces should feel tactile and satisfying -- like arranging ingredients
    on a real workbench, not filling slots in a grid.
  text: |
    UI mockup of the Workshop/Crafting screen -- where players craft items
    from gathered materials.

    LAYOUT: The crafting interface is presented as looking down at a workbench
    from above. The bench surface IS the UI background -- warm wood grain
    texture in honey oak (#C8A96E) with tool marks and stain rings.

    LEFT PANEL (Recipe Book):
    - An open book lying on the bench, pages slightly yellowed parchment.
    - Left page: Recipe list by category (scrollable). Categories as
      hand-drawn section headers: "Woodwork", "Cooking", "Alchemy",
      "Textiles". Each recipe entry shows: name, small icon, tier badge
      (Apprentice/Journeyman/Artisan/Master/Legendary as colored dots).
    - Right page: Selected recipe detail. A larger hand-painted illustration
      of the finished item (a wooden chair, in this mockup). Below:
      ingredient list with icons and quantities. Quality range indicator
      (3-5 stars possible with current materials). Crafting time estimate.

    CENTER (Workbench):
    - Material slots arranged in a natural pattern on the bench (not a grid).
    - 4 ingredient slots shown as shallow carved depressions in the wood.
    - Currently filled: Copperwood Timber x3 (warm reddish wood icons),
      Linseed Oil x1 (amber bottle icon), empty slot, empty slot.
    - A "Craft" button styled as a large wooden mallet resting on the bench.
      Warm green highlight when all required ingredients are placed.

    RIGHT PANEL (Inventory):
    - The player's satchel, open, showing available materials in a flowing
      arrangement (not a rigid grid). Materials organized by type with
      hand-drawn dividers. Each material shows: painted icon, name,
      quantity, quality tier (star color).

    BOTTOM BAR:
    - Currently crafting: "Copperwood Chair" progress indicator styled as
      a hand-drawn progress bar that fills with warm amber. "2:30 remaining."
    - Skill level: "Woodwork: Journeyman (67/100)" rendered as a painted
      progress badge.

    ACTIVE RECIPE DETAIL (shown on the book):
    - "Copperwood Chair"
    - Tier: Journeyman
    - Ingredients: Copperwood Timber x4, Linseed Oil x1, Iron Nails x12
    - Quality: 3-4 stars (based on material quality)
    - Value: ~85 Credits
    - "A chair that remembers the forest it came from. Sits in warmth."

    MOOD: The satisfaction of making something with your hands. The workbench
    is inviting -- you want to put things on it and see what happens. Tools
    hang on the wall behind (visible above the bench): chisels, saws,
    planes, each one a small painting.

    STYLE: The most tactile UI in the game. The wood grain, the carved
    depressions, the worn book pages -- every surface should feel touchable.
    Warm afternoon light illuminating the bench from a window implied above.
  provider_options:
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"
    style: "natural"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

tags: [ui, workshop, crafting, interface, mockup, workbench, game-design]
